      "natural_statement": "For any finite Euclidean dimension, a globally injective Borel map on a Borel set, covered by restrictions of C1 local diffeomorphisms, with continuous positive input/output densities u,v and v(Ta)*abs(det DT(a))/u(a)>=j>0, pushes u da restricted to that set to at most j^(-1)*v da. Countably many disjoint pieces contribute multiplicity one.",
