      },
      "natural_statement": "For every eta>0, the full controlled-volume switching theorem holds with sum B_k^16 finite, at most exp(C*B_k*n) partition cells, original pair-law retained mass at least 1-eta, uniform past/future shadowing error tending to zero, and Phi_*(rho_k restricted to G_k)<=K_k*rho_k for K_k tending to one. Thus its first output marginal is <=K_k*nu, for C^{1,alpha} diffeomorphisms preserving continuous strictly positive densities, including boundary.",
      "formal_statement": "",
